1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,697
The project now demonstrates every boundary of a hierarchical native speaker except one.

2
00:00:05,697 --> 00:00:08,416
Text and seed can choose a finite program.

3
00:00:08,416 --> 00:00:11,524
Persistent tokens can own a coherent trajectory.

4
00:00:11,524 --> 00:00:15,020
A program can expand to exact-count continuous Jewels.

5
00:00:15,020 --> 00:00:19,746
A factorized physical vocabulary can render an irregular spacetime field.

6
00:00:19,746 --> 00:00:23,372
Causal text controls beat shuffled and null generations.

7
00:00:23,372 --> 00:00:31,205
The missing step is replacing source-backed macro tokens with reusable learned object, motion, and background prototypes.

8
00:00:31,905 --> 00:00:38,085
Today, foreground token seven ultimately expands to a constellation derived from one training field.

9
00:00:38,085 --> 00:00:46,057
Composing it with a distinct background proves that the system is not retrieving one complete video, but it still limits novelty.

10
00:00:46,057 --> 00:00:52,916
Scaling eighteen source identifiers to eighteen thousand would memorize more examples, not discover a language.

11
00:00:52,916 --> 00:01:01,444
The next vocabulary must pool recurring connected spacetime tubes across many videos and assign prototypes independent of source identity.

12
00:01:02,144 --> 00:01:08,797
The next experiment fits at least one hundred prompted fields spanning ten to twenty compositional prompts.

13
00:01:08,797 --> 00:01:14,642
It learns sixty-four to two-hundred-fifty-six foreground and background trajectory prototypes.

14
00:01:14,642 --> 00:01:24,031
Each prototype owns a connected tube, but decodes through the existing one-thousand-and-twenty-four-way covariance, surface, and gradient vocabularies.

15
00:01:24,031 --> 00:01:33,233
A no-copy audit rejects any generated macro token that references a source identifier or inherits more than a preregistered fraction from one field.

16
00:01:33,933 --> 00:01:39,118
The full speaker should not autoregress seventy-two thousand independent Jewels.

17
00:01:39,118 --> 00:01:53,766
It should emit a typed hierarchy: scene, style, and camera; persistent object and background identities; trajectory anchors and derivatives; addressed local constellation phrases; then continuous centroids and physical tokens.

18
00:01:53,766 --> 00:01:57,071
A small transformer can model the discrete program.

19
00:01:57,071 --> 00:02:03,553
Specialized differentiable realizers can enforce geometry, exact counts, and support-safe rendering.

20
00:02:03,553 --> 00:02:10,293
This division spends sequence-model capacity on semantic dependencies instead of raster-like repetition.

21
00:02:10,993 --> 00:02:14,071
A class-level path is too rigid for a complete model.

22
00:02:14,071 --> 00:02:21,505
Instead the speaker should emit trajectory anchors together with velocity, and eventually acceleration or spline control points.

23
00:02:21,505 --> 00:02:26,964
Position in the next window is predicted from carried state rather than reset from a template.

24
00:02:26,964 --> 00:02:34,863
Derivatives compactly express direction and continuity, while local Jewel phrases decorate the moving tube with appearance and geometry.

25
00:02:34,863 --> 00:02:43,516
This is why the derivative method outperformed raw local coordinates in the earlier experiments: it assigns the model the temporally stable quantity.

26
00:02:44,216 --> 00:02:50,134
Training and evaluation prompts must be split by object-action combination, not random video.

27
00:02:50,134 --> 00:02:55,161
Correct text must beat cyclic object and action swaps on held-out compositions.

28
00:02:55,161 --> 00:03:00,188
Every prompt needs at least two recognizable but structurally distinct samples.

29
00:03:00,188 --> 00:03:07,887
A second window must continue identity and velocity from generated carry alone, with no target field or teacher scaffold.

30
00:03:07,887 --> 00:03:14,632
These gates distinguish real language scaling from memorization, evaluator bias, and single-window tricks.

31
00:03:15,332 --> 00:03:20,290
More compute is useful only after the representation assigns it the right job.

32
00:03:20,290 --> 00:03:25,058
Data buys repeated examples of objects, actions, cameras, and trajectories.

33
00:03:25,058 --> 00:03:29,698
Prototype learning converts those repetitions into reusable macro tokens.

34
00:03:29,698 --> 00:03:35,102
Program-model compute learns prompt-to-token composition and long-range dependencies.

35
00:03:35,102 --> 00:03:39,678
Rendering compute improves local Jewel realization and support indexing.

36
00:03:39,678 --> 00:03:44,637
The pitch is therefore not that a larger model will rescue independent splats.

37
00:03:44,637 --> 00:03:54,553
It is that every interface is now demonstrated, and scale targets the one unproven interface: reusable vocabulary breadth and cross-window program modeling.
